Z||000026||chester||12-21-2001||09:20 AM||||Well I've already started on my "winter" projects;<P>1) Replace thrashed front coilovers and crossmember. - DONE<P>2) Install stereo components; Rockford Fosgate 1000.1 plate hooked to a Rockford Fosgate 10' HX-2 sub in Aus's center console, Aus's door pods with Polk/Momo seperates, LCD display with TV tuner and bullet camera facing towards rear of car (hi tech rear view mirror   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). 2 Farad stiffening cap. Haven't found a 6 channel amp that I care for yet.<P>3) Redo door panels in black leather on bottoms.  Install Mr Mikes leather seat covers.  Install new dash and glove box. Install new shifter and brake boots. Install remaining marble dash inserts.<P>4) Repin new wiring harness and install Accel programmable ECM.  <P>5) Remove headers and ship to Steve Hamm for turbo cossoverpipe fabrication.<P>6) Install t4 turbo and have car dyno tuned.<P>7) Shave door handles and install electric door latches.<P>8) Install Alpine security system and wire door latches for remote open.<P>9) Install new wing and integrated rocker panels/scoops and paint.<P>I'm sure I missed a few things. Elvira will be glad when I FINALLY empty the closet of all my Fiero parts and get them installed.  I accumulated all parts during the summer and refused to take the car off the road (even with the thrashed suspension) to finish the show season. I don't know if the winter will be long enough to get all this done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> . Now if I can only plug up all the drafts in this shitty garage that I have and get Elvira's car out of it, I'd be golden!<P>Rob D. <P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">        <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension<p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 12-21-2001).]||||reg||1
