Z||000028||Formula88||12-21-2001||10:37 AM||||Getting my Formula ready for show season:<P>New brakes all around<BR>Finish trim painting<BR>-sail panels<BR>-rear bumper moulding<BR>-door sill moulding (needs scratch repair too)<BR>-side view mirrors<BR>Polish and possibly repaint/powdercoat OEM wheels<BR>Touch up bad spots in clear coat - possibly repaint entire car, but probably not.<BR>Restore and install GT exhaust trumpets<BR>New rear bumper 'Pontiac' emblem<BR>Lube power windows and door locks<BR>New sound system-good speakers and OEM UP3 radio (I have the OEM AM/FM cassette for shows)<BR>Recover or replace worn GT steering wheel<BR>Repaint plenum & valve covers<BR>Repair cruise control<BR>Port or replace exhaust manifolds (maybe)<BR>Replace exhaust head pipe (possibly head pipe and new hi-flow cat, possibly entire new West Coast 2.5" exhaust with Spin Tech)<BR>Fix temp gauge/lite wiring factory screwup<BR>Fix innacurate fuel gauge<P><BR>And people wonder why I spend so much time working on my car?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Sorry for the huge list, I'm making this list as much for myself as anything else.  Man, I need to get busy!||||reg||1
