Z||000048||grgoyl86||12-23-2001||09:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>Im not jealous at all.  that garage aint nothin'........   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><BR>how much did that cost,  and how much did you do yourself?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>We had the "shell" built (pole building) for about $11,000. Been working at the rest ourselves, with some help from friends. Got about another $8,000 into it, so far. Electricity, interior walls, paint, insulation, benches, etc. Still needs a ceiling and heat, more storage . . .<P>Will it ever be done?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000049||2M4 Dale||12-23-2001||12:06 PM||||Get kenny86GT potty trained.....then just watch my grand daughter grow normally ... lol<P>But seriously my winter projects are :<P>1. Finish insullation and pegboard in garage...install shelving and build my mega-workbench...finish wiring and complete air compressor installation. (I got a 7hp-60 gallon vertical Porter Cable Compressor for Christmas....life is good !!!)<P>2. Get the 56 Pontiac Wagon road worthy.....rebuild brake systems and rebuild fuel systems.....not to much there really ! About 10-20 hours work and about 200-300 bucks........paint and trim will have to wait.<P>3. Do 2.8 V6 conversion on my 87 coupe. Can't afford the V8 thing this year....The V8 conversion is still in my future plans..but much later and into a different Fiero.<P>4. Mr Mikes leather seat covers.<P>5. Get proffesional buff job on the coupe. (RogerGarrison...do you do this ???)<P>6. Keep on dreaming up new things that I can't afford to do ... LMAO<BR>||||reg||1
